.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH terminal-of-tinsel-packs 1  "packs " 
.SH NAME
terminal\-of\-tinsel\-packs \- List the packs of creatures, or make your own
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBterminal\-of\-tinsel packs\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-color\fR] [\fB\-\-pack\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fIsubcommands\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Creatures come in packs. Use \-\-pack with any command to keep to some of them, e.g. \*(Aqterminal\-of\-tinsel quiz \-\-pack nordic\*(Aq.
.PP
Community packs live in the \*(Aqpacks\*(Aq folder of your config directory and load automatically. \*(Aqpacks new <id>\*(Aq makes one with an example creature to edit. Broken files are skipped with a warning.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Print the command\*(Aqs data as JSON instead of drawing it (errors become a JSON object on stderr)
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-color\fR
Plain output: no colour, no emoji, ASCII borders (also set by NO_COLOR, or by piping)
.TP
\fB\-\-pack\fR \fI<PACK>\fR
Only use creatures from these packs, e.g. \-\-pack nordic,dickens
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
terminal\-of\-tinsel\-packs\-new(1)
Make a community pack with an example creature to edit
